From: Plain Browser
Subject: [safebrowsing] Settings: a Safe Browsing toggle under You and Google, no Enhanced protection, proxy wording

Category: 70-safebrowsing. The only Google service the browser still talks to is Safe Browsing, through our
proxy (0001). Settings > You and Google > Google services gets a plain on/off toggle for it, bound to
safebrowsing.enabled (the same pref the Security page's radio group drives, so both views agree). On the
Security page the Enhanced protection radio is hidden (its real-time lookups are not something the proxy
supports and docs/PRIVACY.md promises it cannot be turned on), the Standard radio loses its collapse (only the
reporting toggle lived there; reporting is disabled by the iridium patches) and the Standard / No protection
descriptions say where requests go. Polish translations are added to generated_resources_pl.xtb with ids
computed the way grit does (first 64 bits of the MD5 of the English text, sign bit stripped).
---
