     </message>
+    <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_PLAINBROWSER_SAFEBROWSING_PROXY" desc="Label of the Safe Browsing toggle on the Google services page">
+      Safe Browsing through the Plain Browser proxy
+    </message>
+    <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_PLAINBROWSER_SAFEBROWSING_PROXY_DESC" desc="Description of the Safe Browsing toggle on the Google services page">
+      Checks the sites you visit against a local copy of Google's Safe Browsing list. The list updates go through sb.plain-browser.app, so Google does not see your IP address or the sites you visit.
+    </message>
     <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_SAFEBROWSING_STANDARD" desc="Label for safe browsing standard protection mode">
       Standard protection
     </message>
     <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_SAFEBROWSING_STANDARD_DESC" desc="Description for safe browsing standard protection mode">
-      Protects against sites, downloads, and extensions that are known to be dangerous. If a page does something suspicious, URLs and bits of page content are sent to Google Safe Browsing.
+      Protects against sites, downloads, and extensions that are known to be dangerous. The check runs against a list stored on your device; the list updates go through the Plain Browser proxy, so Google does not see your IP address or the sites you visit.
     </message>
@@ -1746,5 +1752,5 @@
